# The gate's cpu-spinners row and the GUI form of INV-0269-1 (TASK-26 Q7;
# ADR-0264, ADR-0269, ADR-0268 point 3; INV-0264-3's GUI half). Coordinates
# as tests/gui/limits.script's (logical, 1024 x 768, scale 1).
#
# 1. INV-0269-1: a terminal launched from the dock in room `project` and the
#    first terminal's shell, which enters the same room, run in ONE job: the
#    room's `--mem 16M` counts the terminal from the dock (about 5.4 MiB) against
#    the memory a hog started from the first terminal can take, which stops at
#    9 MiB and not at 15 (a job of its own would give it almost all 16).
# 2. Two rooms with `--cpu 25%` run two spinners each (the rooms' own programs,
#    from the system image); the key latency of a terminal in `home` is
#    measured by the runner's `latency` step, first with nothing spinning (the
#    baseline) and then with the spinners, and the second may be at most
#    450 ms over the first (both over one screendump read). A smoke test of
#    starvation, not a timing: the runner reads the screen every 150 ms, so a
#    time is a screendump plus whole polls (CI, auto: 169 ms with nothing
#    spinning, 331 ms with the spinners, a fixed 300 ms failed); 450 ms is
#    three more polls, and a starved terminal takes seconds. The kernel's own
#    50 ms bound for an uncapped process next to capped rooms that spin and
#    burst is checked by t_cpu (make test-qemu).
serial init: gui: gpu on its own page
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
type mkdir project\r
screen ~> _
type mkdir other\r
screen ~> _
type room new project --mem 16M --procs 6 +w ~/project\r
screen project --colour 1 --mem 16M --procs 6 +w ~/project
screen ~> _
# The dock's chip enters the room; System+Enter launches a terminal in it.
clickc 2f7f8f 300 719 600 7
chord meta ret
origin 105 138
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
prefix project ~/project> _
click 400 120
type memhog\r
prefix memhog: refused after 9
prefix project ~/project> _
# The first terminal's shell enters the same room: a hog started there is
# refused at the same point, since the room has one job.
click 400 80
region 130 76 100 4 f7f7f8
origin 73 106
type room project\r
prefix project ~/project> _
type memhog\r
prefix memhog: refused after 9
prefix project ~/project> _
shot one-job
type room --leave\r
type cd /\r
prefix /> _
# The baseline: a keystroke's latency in home with nothing spinning. Then
# two rooms at 25% with two spinners each, and the latency again.
chord ctrl l
top /> _
pause 1500
latency 10
type room new spin1 --cpu 25% --procs 6 +w ~/other\r
prefix spin1 --colour
prefix /> _
type room new spin2 --cpu 25% --procs 6 +w ~/other\r
prefix spin2 --colour
prefix /> _
type room spin1\r
type spin &\r
prefix [1] spin
type spin &\r
prefix [2] spin
type jobs\r
prefix [1]  running   spin
prefix [2]  running   spin
type room --leave\r
type cd /\r
prefix /> _
chord ctrl l
top /> _
type room spin2\r
type spin &\r
prefix [3] spin
type spin &\r
prefix [4] spin
type room --leave\r
type cd /\r
prefix /> _
chord ctrl l
top /> _
pause 1500
latency 10 +450
shot spinners
type poweroff\r
exit
